22 0 obj
<< /A 262 0 R /Alt (Flowchart depicting responses to threat or chronic stress. A black rectangle labeled \215Threat or chronic stress\216 connects to a green rectangle labeled \215Communication and social engagement \(ventral vagus nerve\)\216 and a yellow rectangle labeled \215Fight or flight-mobilization \(sympathetic system\).\216 A gray rectangle labeled \215No resolution or imminent death\216 connects to a red rectangle labeled \215Immobilization with fear, shutdown or dissociation \(dorsal vagus nerve\).") /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 263 0 R /Alt (Diagram with three overlapping ovals titled \215Transdiagnostic Clinical Phenomena,\216 \215Theoretical Mechanisms Integrated in the SPI,\216 and \215Practical Components of the SPI.\216 The first includes dissociation, emotion dysregulation, alexithymia, autonomic hyper/hypoarousal. The second includes interoception, neuroception, presence, agency, somatic marker hypothesis, embodiment. The third includes grounding, somatopsyche mapping, somatopsyche agency, insight and meditation, gratitude and celebration.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 264 0 R /Alt (Table outlining a seven-step process with goals and probable outcomes. Steps include Grounding, Somatopsychic Mapping, Agency, Remapping, Insight, Mindfulness, and Closure. Goals focus on security, proprioception, transformation, perception enhancement, problem-solving, and integration. Outcomes involve feelings of security, GABAergic activity, mobilization, sympathetic regulation, fearlessness, and oxytocin activity.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
